<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
    <!--
    This file contains suppressions for false positives identified by OWASP Dependency-Check.

    Each suppression should include:
    - A clear comment explaining why it's a false positive
    - The CVE or vulnerability ID
    - The affected dependency (GAV coordinates)
    - A notes field documenting the reason for suppression
    - An expiration date (until) to force periodic review

    Suppression format:
    <suppress>
       <notes><![CDATA[
       Explanation of why this is suppressed
       ]]></notes>
       <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/group\.id/artifact\-id@.*$</packageUrl>
       <cve>CVE-YYYY-NNNNN</cve>
       <until>YYYY-MM-DD</until>
    </suppress>

    For more information, see:
    https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html
    -->

    <!-- Example suppression (remove this when adding real suppressions):
    <suppress>
       <notes><![CDATA[
       CVE-2023-12345 affects version 1.x but we use 2.x which has the fix.
       This is a false positive due to incorrect version detection.
       ]]></notes>
       <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.example/example\-lib@.*$</packageUrl>
       <cve>CVE-2023-12345</cve>
       <until>2026-01-01</until>
    </suppress>
    -->

    <!--
    AWS CDK and Constructs Library Suppressions

    Note: The AWS CDK libraries are well-maintained by Amazon and receive regular security updates.
    Any CVEs found should be carefully evaluated before suppression. Only suppress if:
    1. The CVE affects a transitive dependency not used by CDK
    2. The CVE is fixed in the version we're using (version detection error)
    3. The CVE doesn't apply to our usage pattern
    -->

    <!--
    If you identify false positives during scanning, add them here following the format above.
    Always include:
    - Clear explanation in notes
    - Expiration date for periodic review
    - Specific CVE or vulnerability ID
    -->

    <!--
    AWS CDK Asset False Positives:

    The cdk-asset-awscli-v1 package bundles the AWS CLI as a Lambda layer which includes
    compressed JSON data files (endpoint-rule-set-1.json.gz, service-2.json.gz, etc.).
    The dependency scanner is incorrectly flagging these JSON data files as if they were
    vulnerable Ruby JSON gems or JavaScript packages.

    These are NOT actual code dependencies - they are data files used by the AWS CLI.
    The vulnerabilities CVE-2020-10663 (Ruby JSON gem) and CVE-2021-23497 (JavaScript
    @strikeentco/set package) do not apply to this project which is a Java/Maven project
    that uses AWS CDK.

    Verified: These are compressed JSON configuration files for AWS service endpoints,
    not executable code or library dependencies.
    -->

    <suppress until="2026-11-01Z">
       <notes><![CDATA[
       FALSE POSITIVE: CVE-2020-10663 affects the Ruby JSON gem, but this detection is
       from compressed JSON data files (endpoint-rule-set-1.json.gz, service-2.json.gz, etc.)
       inside the AWS CLI layer bundled with cdk-asset-awscli-v1.
       These are not Ruby gems or executable code - they are static configuration files.
       This project does not use Ruby or the Ruby JSON gem.
       ]]></notes>
       <filePath regex="true">.*cdk-asset-awscli-v1.*\.json\.gz$</filePath>
       <cve>CVE-2020-10663</cve>
    </suppress>

    <suppress until="2026-11-01Z">
       <notes><![CDATA[
       FALSE POSITIVE: CVE-2021-23497 affects the JavaScript package @strikeentco/set,
       but this detection is from compressed JSON data files (endpoint-rule-set-1.json.gz)
       inside the AWS CLI layer bundled with cdk-asset-awscli-v1.
       These are not JavaScript packages or executable code - they are static AWS service
       endpoint configuration files.
       This project does not use the @strikeentco/set npm package.
       ]]></notes>
       <filePath regex="true">.*cdk-asset-awscli-v1.*\.json\.gz$</filePath>
       <cve>CVE-2021-23497</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>
